      <p class="legal-p">The Website is operated by {SITE.legalEntity} (ABN {SITE.abn}), trading as ALYRA (“ALYRA”, “we”, “us” or “our”).</p>
      <p class="legal-p">ALYRA provides loans to private clients secured against pledged high-value assets, under applicable pawnbroking laws. ALYRA holds a pawnbroker licence and second-hand dealer registration in {SITE.pawnbrokerLicenceJurisdiction}. Our <a href="/licence/">Licensing &amp; Registration</a> page sets out the details that apply.</p>

      <h2 class="legal-h2">3. General information only</h2>
      <p class="legal-p legal-p--em">The information on the Website is general in nature. It is provided for information purposes only and does not take into account your personal circumstances, objectives, financial situation or needs.</p>
      <p class="legal-p">Nothing on the Website constitutes, or should be relied on as:</p>
      <ul class="legal-list">
        <li>financial, legal, tax, credit or investment advice;</li>
        <li>a valuation or appraisal of any particular asset;</li>
        <li>a recommendation that a loan or other product is suitable for you; or</li>
        <li>a statement that any particular asset would be accepted, or that any particular amount would be lent against it.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="legal-p">You should consider whether the information is appropriate to your circumstances and obtain independent professional advice before making any decision.</p>

      <h2 class="legal-h2">4. No offer</h2>
      <p class="legal-p legal-p--em">Nothing on the Website is an offer to lend, an invitation to apply for credit, or an agreement to enter into any transaction.</p>
      <p class="legal-p">Loan amounts, ranges, loan-to-value indications, timeframes and examples shown on the Website are illustrative only. Each enquiry is assessed individually, and ALYRA may decline any enquiry at its discretion and without giving reasons.</p>
      <p class="legal-p">Nothing on the Website creates a binding obligation on ALYRA to value, accept, lend against, purchase, hold or return any asset. Any such obligation arises only under a written agreement signed by ALYRA.</p>

      <h2 class="legal-h2">5. Loans are governed by separate written terms</h2>
      <p class="legal-p">If you proceed with a loan or other transaction, it will be governed by the written agreement and any related documents provided to you directly, which prevail over these Terms to the extent of any inconsistency.</p>
      <p class="legal-p">Before you proceed with a loan, we will disclose to you the fees, interest, repayment terms, notices, redemption rights and enforcement processes that apply.</p>
      <p class="legal-p legal-p--em">A loan secured against a pledged asset places that asset at risk. If you do not meet your repayment obligations, the asset may be sold in accordance with the loan agreement and applicable law.</p>
      <p class="legal-p">Please read any agreement carefully and seek independent advice if you are unsure about any part of it.</p>

      <h2 class="legal-h2">6. Enquiries and confidential valuations</h2>
      <p class="legal-p">The Website allows you to make a general enquiry or request a confidential valuation of an asset. When you do so:</p>
      <ul class="legal-list">
        <li>you must provide information that is accurate, complete and not misleading;</li>
        <li>you confirm that you own the asset, or are authorised by the owner to deal with it and to provide information about it;</li>
